    target: has exactly one colored marker pixel at canonical offset (k_max, k_max) rotated to its kind, where k_max is the pattern's largest inward-diagonal k. Marker color is that corner's output color; it may repeat across corners/frames.
  transform (input -> output):
    for every target corner, paint the canonical pattern (rotated to that corner's TL/TR/BL/BR orientation) using that corner's marker color, onto bg/0 cells (marker pixel is preserved/overwritten with same color)

